      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T05:14:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let’s get @archana.kakani@ibm.com input on this PDI comment: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/94606/comment/bb0620d9_67710d11/\n\nFor SPDM 1.2, Redfish SignedMeasurements includes the VCA and the GET_MEASUREMENTS request/response transcript, including any opaque data in the MEASUREMENTS responses. I’d like to better understand the use case for exposing this property additionally.",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18c09e1f_63be5bc0",
        "filename": "requester/component_integrity_dbus.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 377,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003188
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:18:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that SignedMeasurements already contains these bytes. The reason for\nthis change is that merged PDI change 94606 already exposes a separate\nOpaqueData result, but the requester currently always returns an empty array,\neven when a responder supplies non-empty opaque data. This patch forwards the\nactual bytes from the final signed response so that the existing D-Bus result\naccurately reflects the response.",
      "parentUuid": "3d227e82_3faf5f03",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bbb07db_1ef9208c",
        "filename": "requester/component_integrity_dbus.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003181
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T04:13:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that libspdm 3.8.2 rejects the opaque data if opaque_length \u003e\u003d buffer size. So with this 1024 byte buffer, a device sending the full 1024 bytes will fail with BUFFER_TOO_SMALL. I see libspdm maintainers already fixed this on main https://github.com/DMTF/libspdm/commit/cd06c89ed3c1e8c3205e8206cab191f1d297f310\nbut it\u0027s not in a release yet",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "36f49ffb_baaa8e3d",
        "filename": "requester/component_integrity_dbus.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003188
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:18:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Allocated SPDM_MAX_OPAQUE_DATA_SIZE + 1 bytes to accommodate libspdm 3.8.2\u0027s\nstrict capacity check, while still rejecting returned data above the protocol\nmaximum. Added tests for a full 1024-byte payload under both the old and fixed\nchecks, and for rejecting an oversized payload.",
      "parentUuid": "6bbb07db_1ef9208c",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2a3075f_74e9e8f5",
        "filename": "requester/component_integrity_dbus.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 592,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003181
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T04:13:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we keep this Unknown until the certificate is verified against a trusted root? spdmd doesn’t provision one today. Also, LIBSPDM_STATUS_VERIF_NO_AUTHORITY is a warning for a root mismatch, so getCertificate() LIBSPDM_STATUS_IS_ERROR check would miss it even after provisioning. A valid measurement signature alone doesn’t establish a trusted identity. \nRef - https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/ComponentIntegrity.v1_4_0.json",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df5f2b72_5ef23dad",
        "filename": "requester/component_integrity_dbus.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 592,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003188
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T09:18:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. ResponderVerificationStatus now stays Unknown because the requester\ndoes not provision a trusted root. Successful evidence collection updates\nLastUpdated without establishing a trusted identity. Added coverage for both\na successful certificate result and LIBSPDM_STATUS_VERIF_NO_AUTHORITY.",
      "parentUuid": "d2a3075f_74e9e8f5",
      "revId": "ca27f1e372eeeda42afdb793885e7caa4bd1845b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
